ior to eating out at a restaurant . she can also use zofran if needed . however , i have encouraged her to reduce greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption . i have asked her to follow up in one month by emailing over mychart regarding any side effects and issues , or issues with elavil or if adjustments are needed .\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient has a history of Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) and Functional Abdominal Pain.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient reports that she goes out to eat on Friday and Saturday nights and has been eating spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She has also been drinking with her friends.\n\nFAMILY HISTORY\n\nThe patient reports that she has a family history of gastrointestinal problems.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\nThe patient was prescribed Bentyl 20 mg as needed for intestinal cramping. She was also prescribed Reglan 10 mg as needed for nausea, but she has not been using it. She was prescribed Zofran as needed for nausea.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Reports flares of abdominal pain.\nGastrointestinal: Reports diarrhea, nausea, and abdominal pain.\nMusculoskeletal: Reports abdominal pain.\nPsychiatric: Reports stress.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nConstitutional: Alert and cooperative, stated age.\nRespiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.\nCardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm.\nGastrointestinal: Soft, non-tender abdomen, no masses or organomegaly, normal active bowel sounds.\n\nRESULTS\n\nNone.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nBrittany Edwards is a pleasant 32-year-old female who was last seen in August of 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with Irritable Bowel Syndrome. She was previously prescribed Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl 