ormed today. The study shows disk desiccation, disk bulge with paracentral disk herniation resulting in moderate right neuroforaminal stenosis.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nLumbar back pain at the L4-L5 disk space due to a herniated disk with radiculopathy.\n\nPatient understanding and agreement: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended plan.\n\nPatient education and counseling: I discussed the results of his MRI and the recommended treatment options with the patient today. He understands that the MRI shows a herniated disk and that we will be performing a spinal injection with a steroid and a strong NSAID today.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\n• We will be performing a spinal injection with a steroid and a strong NSAID today. He understands that this is a typical procedure and that the risks are minimal.\n• We will provide the patient with paperwork that explains the procedure in more detail. If he has any further questions, he can reach out to us.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\n• We will be performing a spinal injection with a steroid and a strong NSAID today. He understands that this is a typical procedure and that the risks are minimal.\n• We will provide the patient with paperwork that explains the procedure in more detail. If he has any further questions, he can reach out to us. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nKyle Morales is a pleasant 58-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of low back pain.\n\nOnset of his pain began 2 weeks ago, when he was lifting a box of books and felt a pop. The pain is described as aching and sharp. His pain has been increasing since the time of onset and is beginning to radiate down his left leg. The patient denies any pain with sitting. He adds that he has a sedentary job. The patient states that his pain does not 